\title{The kernel does not finish the proof that block 15 of \code{\verb~|expf~} computes \code{\verb~|expfMain~}}
\taxon{Problem}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{exp}
\tag{kernel}
\meta{status}{superseded}
\meta{created}{2026-11-23}
\meta{updated}{2026-11-24}
\meta{pr}{12}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} superseded by [dec-03IY](dec-03IY) and \pr{17}. Direct Clang-AST extraction (\code{\verb~|ast2lean~}, \pr{15}) produces high-level functional Lean kernels over \code{\verb~|LibcMath.Core~} directly; the legacy IR interpreter and \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Extracted/ExpfStructured*.lean~} (along with \code{\verb~|Block15ComputesExpfMain~}) were removed in \pr{17} ([log-GHTT](log-GHTT)).}
\p{\code{\verb~|Block15ComputesExpfMain~} in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Extracted/ExpfStructuredOpen.lean~} says that from block 15 on the interpreter computes \code{\verb~|expfMain~}, for every argument and rounding direction. It is a hypothesis of \code{\verb~|runUnary_eq_expfStructured~} and of \code{\verb~|holdsOnBits_of_checkBlockMain'~}, so the faster check on the structured form ([log-Q3D3](log-Q3D3)) does not yet give a theorem about the extracted code.}
\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|LibcMath/Extracted/ExpfStructuredExec.lean~} has a proof in which every tactic step elaborates. According to the description of \pr{12}, the kernel checks the first 8 of the 22 instructions of block 20 in seconds and did not finish the whole within 25 minutes on a loaded machine; whether it terminates is not known. The file is not imported, and was not built by the session that merged it.}
\li{The same description records two traps in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/IR/InterpLemmas.lean~}: simplifying a whole block under \code{\verb~|Option.bind~} is exponential in its length, and \code{\verb~|Option.bind_eq_bind~} as a \code{\verb~|rfl~} lemma leaves the kernel to compare the two forms by unfolding.}
\li{To try: split block 20 into lemmas of a few instructions each, so that the kernel checks short terms; or prove the equality by the method of the short paths in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Extracted/ExpfPaths/Exec.lean~}.}
\li{The structured form is also what a bound on the error of this path would be stated about.}
}
